      "The correct answer is C",
      "I concur with C",
      "A-SIEM is the correct answer\n“Security information and event management (SIEM) software provides a centralized repository for logs, audit events, and security device alerts to detect and notify admins of suspicious activity. For example, attackers can enable a backdoor on a compromised device that will provide them with undetected access for long periods of time; this problem is often solved by applying patches, but SIEM solutions may detect repeated abnormal login times to a server.”",
      "Sorry, meant C is the correct answer. SIEM logs",
