    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 43,
    "question": "A technician is trying to determine the reason why a Linux server is not communicating on a network. The returned network configuration is as follows: eth0: flags=4163<UP,BROADCAST,RUNNING,MULTICAST> mtu 1500 inet 127.0.0.1 network 255.255.0.0 broadcast 127.0.0.1\nWhich of the following BEST describes what is happening?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The server is configured to use DHCP on a network that has multiple scope options",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The server is configured to use DHCP, but the DHCP server is sending an incorrect subnet mask",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The server is configured to use DHCP on a network that does not have a DHCP server",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The server is configured to use DHCP, but the DHCP server is sending an incorrect MTU setting",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "I think it's C",
      "If the network does not have a DHCP server then the server should get APIPA that self-assigned address when the client fails to lease an address from a DHCP server.",
      "Correct Answer:\n✅ C. The server is configured to use DHCP on a network that does not have a DHCP server",
      "It's evident that the server's network interface eth0 is configured with the IP address 127.0.0.1, which is the loopback address. This address is reserved for communication within the local system and is not used for external network communication. Additionally, the subnet mask 255.255.0.0 is associated with this loopback address.\n\nGiven this information, the most suitable explanation is:\n\nC. The server is configured to use DHCP on a network that does not have a DHCP server.\n\nThe Server will not get an APIPA address because this is a Linux server",
      "If the network does not have a DHCP server then the server should get APIPA that self-assigned address when the client fails to lease an address from a DHCP server.",
      "I think provided answer (B) is correct\nThe loopback interface should be assigned a netmask of 255.0.0.0, since 127.0.0.1 is a class A address.\nRef: https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/linux-network-administrators/1565924002/ch05s07.html"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/73222-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-43-discussion/"
  },
