    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The WinSCP tool is commonly used to transfer files between Linux and Windows systems. WinSCP has an easy GUI and encrypts the contents of the file transfer.",
      "SCP\nLinux also relies on scp to provide encrypted file transfers using SSH. The Linux command to copy a file is cp. Therefore, scp is secure copy. It uses the same encryption mechanism as SSH to guarantee file integrity and confidentiality.\n\nIf there is WinSCP available, WinSCP is the best answer.\nThe WinSCP tool is commonly used to transfer files between Linux and Windows systems. WinSCP has an easy GUI and encrypts the contents of the file transfer.\n\nRef. The Official CompTIA Server+ Study Guide (Exam SK0-005) page 198.",
      "Xcopy and Robocopy are two Windows built-in command line file copy utilities. Both of them can help you copy files and folders from one location to another.",
      "https://winscp.net/eng/docs/transfer_mode",
      "Also, robocopy & xcopy are windows os only commands for windows machines, telnet is irrelevant"
    ],
