  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 50,
    "question": "Which of the following DR testing scenarios is described as verbally walking through each step of the DR plan in the context of a meeting?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Live failover",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Simulated failover",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Asynchronous",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Tabletop",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Tabletop is more appropriate",
      "Tabletop",
      ". Tabletop is the DR testing scenario that is described as verbally walking through each step of the DR plan in the context of a meeting. This type of test is often used to evaluate the effectiveness of a disaster recovery plan and to identify areas for improvement. It involves a group of stakeholders discussing hypothetical scenarios and the steps they would take to respond to them, without actually executing any of the recovery procedures",
      "D. TableTop/Simulated Failover - the DRP are implemented on a limited scale. Participants engage in role-playing to ensure comprehension and realism.",
      "it is def table top",
      "ddddddddddd",
      "D. Tabletop is the DR testing scenario that is described as verbally walking through each step of the DR plan in the context of a meeting. This type of test is often used to evaluate the effectiveness of a disaster recovery plan and to identify areas for improvement. It involves a group of stakeholders discussing hypothetical scenarios and the steps they would take to respond to them, without actually executing any of the recovery procedures.",
      "Tabletops\nConducting a tabletop exercise is the most cost-effective and efficient way to identify areas of vulnerability before moving on to more involved testing. A tabletop exercise is an informal brainstorming session that encourages participation from business leaders and other key employees. In a tabletop exercise, the participants agree to determine a particular attack scenario upon which they then focus.\nCompTIA Server+ Study Guide: Exam SK0-005 Chapter 9 Disaster Recovery",
      "Answer is D. A live failover is a real scenario in which an active/active cluster configuration experiences a failure in one of the nodes which results in zero downtime due to the active redundancy of the other nodes.",
      "Tabletop/Simulated failover—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented on a limited scale. Participants engage in role-playing to ensure comprehension and realism.\nParallel recovery using a non-production test environment—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented in a non-production environment. VMs work especially well for this kind of test. The production environment remains unaffected.",
      "Tabletop/Simulated failover—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented on a limited scale. Participants engage in role-playing to ensure comprehension and realism.\nParallel recovery using a non-production test environment—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented in a non-production environment. VMs work especially well for this kind of test. The production environment remains unaffected.",
      "Thinks this one is wrong... Sounds more like Tabletop or even walk through",
      "Paper test—critical stakeholders examine the disaster recovery procedures in the organization, and suggestions are considered.\nWalk-through—the disaster recovery procedures are stepped through to confirm their viability. No changes are made, and no data is restored.\nTabletop/Simulated failover—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented on a limited scale. Participants engage in role-playing to ensure comprehension and realism.\nParallel recovery using a non-production test environment—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented in a non-production environment. VMs work especially well for this kind of test. The production environment remains unaffected.\nLive failover (cutover)—the disaster recovery procedure is tested on the production environment where customers and employees reside. The goal is to prove zero interruption of service."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/71969-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-50-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 51,
    "question": "When configuring networking on a VM, which of the following methods would allow multiple VMs to share the same host IP address?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Bridged",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "NAT",
