  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 106,
    "question": "A server administrator is deploying a UPS at a datacenter and notices the device is making an audible beep every few seconds. Which of the following is the\nMOST likely cause?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The battery cable is disconnected",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The device is plugged into the wrong outlet",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The battery is faulty",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The serial cable is not connected",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C: Faulty battery.\njust replaced one of these this week.",
      "An audible beep from a UPS every few seconds usually indicates a problem with the battery connection or power source. The most common cause is that the battery cable is disconnected, meaning the UPS cannot access its battery backup. This issue often occurs after installation or maintenance when the battery is not properly reconnected.",
      "I think A is the answer.\n\nUPSs make periodic sounds, usually to indicate some problem or anomaly.\nOne of the most common causes is a battery-related problem.\n\nIn this situation, it is wise to first check for the simplest and most likely cause, a poor battery cable connection, since the newly installed UPS is sounding the warning tone. This is an easy fix and often solves the problem.",
      "If you've lost power, it's beeping to let you know that the battery is in use, and that you should save your work and shut down your computer. A constant beep (every second or two, and never stopping) generally means the UPS is very low on battery power, and you should shut down immediately.\n\nOf the following options it is the most likely although the beeps really mean there is a power issue but from which direction... unplugged? bad battery? low battery?\n\nhttps://www.wingswept.com/uninterruptible-power-supply-beeping/#"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/82568-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-106-discussion/"
  },
  {
