  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 201,
    "question": "A server room contains ten physical servers that are running applications and a cluster of three dedicated hypervisors. The hypervisors are new and only have 10% utilization. The Chief Financial Officer has asked that the IT department do what it can to cut back on power consumption and maintenance costs in the data center.\n\nWhich of the following would address the request with minimal server downtime?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Unplug the power cables from the redundant power supplies, leaving just the minimum required.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Convert the physical servers to the hypervisors and retire the ten servers.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Reimage the physical servers and retire all ten servers after the migration is complete.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Convert the ten servers to power-efficient core editions.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Option B, which involves converting the physical servers to the hypervisors and retiring the ten servers, would address the request with minimal server downtime and reduce power consumption and maintenance costs. Since the hypervisors are new and have low utilization, there is ample capacity to virtualize the existing physical servers. This would reduce the number of physical servers, resulting in lower power consumption and maintenance costs.\n\nOption A, which involves unplugging power cables, may result in unexpected downtime and would not reduce power consumption or maintenance costs.\n\nOption C, which involves re-imaging the physical servers and retiring them after the migration is complete, would require significant downtime and would not necessarily reduce power consumption or maintenance costs.\n\nOption D, which involves converting the physical servers to power-efficient core editions, may reduce power consumption, but would not necessarily ad"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/106039-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-201-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 202,
    "question": "A company needs to increase the security controls on its servers. An administrator is implementing MFA on all servers using cost-effective techniques.\n\nWhich of the following should the administrator use to satisfy the MFA requirement?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Biometrics",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Push notifications",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Smart cards",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Physical tokens",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Option B, push notifications, would be the most cost-effective solution to implement MFA on all servers. With push notifications, the user receives a notification on their mobile device or computer prompting them to approve or deny access to the server. This method does not require any additional hardware or tokens and can be implemented easily.\n\nOption A, biometrics, may provide a high level of security, but it would require additional hardware such as fingerprint scanners or facial recognition cameras, which can be expensive.\n\nOption C, smart cards, require the purchase and distribution of smart cards to all users, which can be costly and time-consuming to manage.\n\nOption D, physical tokens, such as key fobs or USB tokens, are also costly to purchase and distribute to all users. Additionally, if a user loses their token, it may cause a delay in access to the server until a new token can be distributed.",
      "agree with B",
      "Option B, push notifications, is likely the most cost-effective technique for implementing MFA on servers. This option involves a user attempting to log in with their username and password, and then receiving a push notification on their mobile device asking them to confirm the login attempt. This provides an additional layer of authentication beyond just a username and password."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/105913-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-202-discussion/"
  },
  {
