  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 218,
    "question": "Which of the following commands would MOST likely be used to register a new service on a Windows OS?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "set-service",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "net",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "sc",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "services.msc",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Going with (C) on the assumption it's a typo meant for \"sc.exe\" (Service Control Manager)\n* \"sc\" (alias for Set-Content) cannot create new services, \"set-service\", \"services.msc\", and \"net\" only modify existing services and objects.",
      "The command that would most likely be used to register a new service on a Windows OS is \"sc\".\n\n\"sc\" is a command-line utility that is used to manage Windows services. It can be used to create, modify, start, stop, and delete services, among other things. The \"create\" command in particular is used to create a new service.\n\nThe other options listed (A, B, and D) are not used specifically for registering new services. \"set-service\" is used to modify the settings of an existing service, \"net\" is used for managing network resources, and \"services.msc\" is a graphical user interface (GUI) tool for managing services.",
      "The SC command is used to configure, query, stop, start, delete, and add system services on the Windows command line. Most of the SC command subcommands apply equally to drivers. If you have the appropriate permissions, the SC command can be used to manage services on both the local and remote systems."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/105453-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-218-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 219,
    "question": "An administrator receives an alert stating a S.M.A.R.T. error has been detected. Which of the following should the administrator run FIRST to determine the issue?",
    "options": [
