  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 237,
    "question": "Which of the following is a type of replication in which all files are replicated, all of the time?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Constant",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Application consistent",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Synthetic full",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Full",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The correct answer is: D. Full\n\n✅ Explanation:\nFull replication (or full backup/replication) means all files are copied every time the replication or backup process runs — regardless of whether they've changed or not.",
      "This is subtly tricky wording. \"All of the time\" sounds like real-time (constant), but in backup and replication terminology, “Full” replication is what replicates all files every time a job runs — regardless of changes.\n\nWhereas Constant replication replicates only the changes, but does so immediately, not necessarily the entire data set every time.",
      "A. Constant",
      "Must be A",
      "ithink the answer is A",
      "You are right.\nThe answer is A. Constant.\nThis is a type of replication in which all files are replicated all the time. Constant replication ensures that the source and the destination are always in sync and that any changes made to the source are immediately reflected on the destination."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/110978-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-237-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 238,
    "question": "A technician installed a kernel upgrade to a Linux server. The server now crashes regularly. Which of the following is the MOST likely cause?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Necessary dependencies were installed for multiple architectures.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "There is not enough hard drive space.",
