    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/128151-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-242-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 243,
    "question": "Which of the following should a technician verify FIRST before decommissioning and wiping a file server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The media destruction method",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The recycling policy",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Asset management documentation",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Non-utilization",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The correct answer is: D. Non-utilization ✅\n\nExplanation:\nBefore wiping and decommissioning a file server, the technician must first verify that the server is no longer in use (non-utilization). This ensures no active users, applications, or business processes are still depending on it.\n\nA. Media destruction method → Important later, but not the first check.\n\nB. Recycling policy → Relevant after confirming decommissioning, not before.\n\nC. Asset management documentation → Good for tracking, but the priority is ensuring the server isn’t still needed.\n\nSo the first step is to verify non-utilization before proceeding with decommissioning and wiping.",
      "Disingenuous on CompTIA's part to preach to \"follow your company's policy\" then push a question like this over an exact order. From what I'm gathering in CompTIA's Server+ Student Guide and run-of-the-mill searches \"C. Asset management documentation\" is the correct answer here.\n*I originally wanted to go with D. but it seems there are some more impactful steps in non-utilization versus documentation.",
      "D. Non-utilization\nverify this first",
      "C. Asset management documentation\n\nC. Asset management documentation:\n\nBefore decommissioning a file server, it's essential to check the asset management documentation.\nAsset management documentation includes details about the server, such as its location, purpose, owner, and any other relevant information. Verifying this documentation helps ensure that the decommissioning process aligns with organizational policies and doesn't lead to unintended consequences, such as the loss of critical information.\n\nMakes more sense to do this before D",
      "Before decommissioning and wiping a file server, the technician should first verify that the server is no longer in use and that no crucial data or services are still relying on it. Therefore, the first thing to verify is:\n\nD. Non-utilization\n\nThis ensures that decommissioning the server won't disrupt any ongoing operations or result in data loss. Once confirmed, other processes like asset management documentation, recycling policies, and media destruction methods can be considered."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/123943-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-243-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 244,
    "question": "A server administrator needs to implement load balancing without purchasing any new hardware or implementing any new software. Which of the following will the administrator MOST likely implement?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Round robin",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Link aggregation",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Most recently used",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Heartbeat",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Only \"Load Balancing\" methods outlined in the \"Load Balancing\" section of the Server+ Student Guide are \"A. Round Robin\" and \"C. Most recently used\".\nGoing with A as C is described as \"attempting\" to use existing machines and can spin up VMs, contradicting the goal of no additional software.",
      "B. Link aggregation",
      "It's B. RR might require new hardware in the form of additional servers. Most servers have more than one NIC and even if it didn't an additional NIC is cheaper than additional server. Also all server need the redundancy and load balancing that NIC teaming offers, only select types need RR.",
      "A. Round robin"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135829-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-244-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 245,
    "question": "A technician is creating a network share that will be used across both Unix and Windows clients at the same time. Users need read and write access to the files. Which of the following would be BEST for the technician to deploy?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "iSCSI",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "CIFS",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "HTTPS",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "DAS",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "B. CIFS\n\nCIFS (Common Internet File System) is a network file-sharing protocol that is widely supported across both Unix/Linux and Windows operating systems. It allows for seamless file sharing and access between different operating systems.",
      "B. CIFS\n\nCIFS (Common Internet File System) is a protocol that allows for file sharing and resource sharing between Unix and Windows clients. It provides compatibility between Unix/Linux-based systems and Windows systems, allowing both types of clients to access shared files and resources on the network."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135432-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-245-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 246,
    "question": "A technician is able to copy a file to a temporary folder on another partition but is unable to copy it to a network share or a USB flash drive. Which of the following is MOST likely preventing the file from being copied to certain locations?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "An ACL",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Antivirus",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "DLP",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "A firewall",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. DLP\n\nData Loss Prevention (DLP):.\nDLP systems are designed to prevent the external loss of sensitive data. It is typical DLP behavior to allow files to be moved internally, but restrict copying to external devices or network shares.",
      "C. DLP"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135830-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-246-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 247,
    "question": "An administrator is helping to replicate a large amount of data between two Windows servers. The administrator is unsure how much data has already been transferred. Which of the following will BEST ensure all the data is copied consistently?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "rsync",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "copy",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "scp",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "robocopy",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. robocopy\n\nRobocopy (Robust File Copy) is a command-line tool built into Windows operating systems that is specifically designed for reliable and efficient file replication and synchronization tasks.\n\n1. Robustness: Robocopy is known for its robustness and reliability. It can handle large amounts of data and is capable of resuming interrupted file transfers without data loss, making it ideal for copying large data sets.\n\n2. Consistency: Robocopy ensures consistency during file replication by copying files in a single operation, preserving file attributes, permissions, timestamps, and other metadata\n\n3. Error Handling: Robocopy provides comprehensive error handling and logging capabilities for issues that may arise during the replication process\n\n4. Performance: While robocopy may not be the fastest file copying tool available, it offers good performance for large data transfers"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135831-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-247-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 248,
    "question": "An administrator notices high traffic on a certain subnet and would like to identify the source of the traffic. Which of the following tools should the administrator utilize?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Anti-malware",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Nbtstat",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Port scanner",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Sniffer",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. Sniffer\n\nExplanation:\nA sniffer (or packet sniffer) is a tool used to capture and analyze network traffic. By inspecting the captured packets, the administrator can identify the IP addresses, protocols, and port numbers associated with the high traffic. This information can help pinpoint the source of the traffic, whether it's due to legitimate network activity, malicious activity, misconfigured devices, or other issues.",
      "D. Sniffer"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/121250-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-248-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 249,
    "question": "Which of the following script types uses commands that start with Set-?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Batch",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Bash",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "PowerShell",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "JavaScript",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. PowerShell\n\nIn PowerShell scripting, commands often start with \"Set-\" to indicate actions related to setting or changing configurations, properties, or values. PowerShell is a powerful scripting language and command-line shell developed by Microsoft specifically for system administration tasks, automation, and configuration management in Windows environments.\n\nCommands starting with \"Set-\" are typically used to modify settings, configurations, or attributes of various system components, such as services, registry entries, environment variables, file permissions, and more. For example, \"Set-Service\" is used to modify the properties of Windows services, \"Set-Item\" is used to modify registry entries or file attributes, and \"Set-Variable\" is used to define or modify variables within PowerShell scripts."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135832-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-249-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 250,
    "question": "A change in policy requires a complete backup of the accounting server every seven days and a backup of modified data every day. Which of the following would be BEST to restore a full backup as quickly as possible in the event of a complete loss of server data?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "A full, weekly backup with daily open-file backups",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "A full, weekly backup with daily archive backups",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "A full, weekly backup with daily incremental backups",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "A full, weekly backup with daily differential backups",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. A full, weekly backup with daily differential backups.",
      "Keyword \"restore\": Incremental will \"backup\" quicker than Differential, but will \"restore\" slower, ergo quickest option is D.",
      "D. A full, weekly backup with daily differential backups\n\nDifferential backups capture all changes made since the last full backup. By performing a full backup of the accounting server every seven days and then creating daily differential backups, you ensure that you have a comprehensive backup of all modified data since the last full backup.\n\nWhen restoring the server data, you only need to restore the last full backup and the latest differential backup. This minimizes the restore time compared to other backup types because you only need to apply the latest differential backup to the full backup to bring the data up to date.",
      "This is the way",
      "To restore a full backup as quickly as possible in the event of a complete loss of server data, you would want to minimize the number of backup sets you need to restore. Given the options:\n\nD. A full, weekly backup with daily differential backups\n\nThis would be the best choice. With differential backups, each backup contains all the changes since the last full backup. So, in the event of a complete loss, you would only need to restore the latest full backup and the latest differential backup. If you were using incremental backups, you would need to restore the full backup and every incremental backup since the last full backup, which would take longer.",
      "Only backing up modified data on a daily basis. Must be incremental."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/112952-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-250-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 251,
    "question": "An administrator has been asked to increase the storage capacity of a stand-alone file server, but no further expansion slots are available. Which of the following would be the FASTEST solution to implement with no downtime?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Configure a RAID array.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Replace the current drives with higher-capacity disks.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Implement FCoE for more storage capacity.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Connect the server to a SAN.",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. Connect the server to a SAN\n\nConnecting the server to a SAN would allow the administrator to expand the storage capacity without downtime by adding additional storage resources from the SAN to the file server without needing to physically replace disks or disrupt server operations. The SAN can provide additional storage capacity without requiring the server to be taken offline. This solution offers scalability and flexibility in expanding storage capacity while minimizing downtime.",
      "Key word is no downtime. A and C are irelevant, and B would cause downtime. D makes most sense here.",
      "I think B is correct"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/117628-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-251-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 252,
    "question": "A Linux server was recently updated. Now, the server stops during the boot process with a blank screen and an fs> prompt. Which of the following is the MOST likely cause of this issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The system is booting to a USB flash drive.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The UEFI boot was interrupted by a missing Linux boot file.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The BIOS could not find a bootable hard disk.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The BIOS firmware needs to be upgraded.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "B. The UEFI boot was interrupted by a missing Linux boot file.\n\nThis is the most likely cause. If the UEFI firmware cannot find the EFI boot loader for Linux (e.g., grubx64.efi or shimx64.efi in the EFI System Partition), it may drop to the UEFI shell (fs>) instead of booting the operating system.\n\nWhen a Linux server stops during the boot process with a blank screen and an fs> prompt, this indicates that the system has entered the UEFI Shell. This usually occurs when the UEFI firmware cannot find a valid boot device or boot file to load the operating system. The fs> prompt is a typical UEFI file system shell prompt, suggesting that the issue is related to UEFI and the boot process."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135833-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-252-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 253,
    "question": "A server technician arrives at a data center to troubleshoot a physical server that is not responding to remote management software. The technician discovers the servers in the data center are not connected to a KVM switch, and their out-of-band management cards have not been configured. Which of the following should the technician do to access the server for troubleshooting purposes?",
