  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 254,
    "question": "Which of the following describes a configuration in which both nodes of a redundant system respond to service requests whenever possible?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Active-passive",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Failover",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Active-active",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Failback",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. Active-active",
      "A is correct answer here\nBoth nodes can respond. In active passive, only 1 node can respond since other is on standby.\nFailover is when node switches to active / failed\nFailback is when failed node returns to service",
      "Per BING..A configuration in which both nodes of a redundant system respond to service requests whenever possible is called an active-active configuration 12. In this configuration, both nodes are active and can respond to service requests. This configuration provides high availability and redundancy in case of a failure of one of the nodes..sounds reasonable"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/124036-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-254-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 255,
    "question": "Users have noticed a server is performing below baseline expectations. While diagnosing the server, an administrator discovers disk drive performance has degraded. The administrator checks the diagnostics on the RAID controller and sees the battery on the controller has gone bad. Which of the following is causing the poor performance on the RAID array?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The controller has disabled the write cache.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The controller cannot use all the available channels.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The drive array is corrupt.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The controller has lost its configuration.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A. The controller has disabled the write cache.\n\nWhen the battery fails, the RAID controller may disable its write cache to prevent data loss in the event of a power failure. Without the cache, every write operation has to be fully completed on the disk before proceeding, significantly slowing down disk operations.",
      "A. The controller has disabled the write cache.\nBattery has a cache that can be used to store data before being wrote onto disk. If battery fails this cache is disabled to avoid data loss incase of a power outage."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/128315-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-255-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
