  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 281,
    "question": "An administrator has been asked to deploy a database server that provides the highest performance with fault tolerance. Which of the following RAID levels will fulfill this request?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "RAID 0",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "RAID 1",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "RAID 5",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "RAID 6",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "E",
        "text": "RAID 10",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "E"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Why RAID 10?\n\nPerformance:\nRAID 10 stripes data across multiple mirrored pairs. Striping (RAID 0) gives very high read/write speed.\nFault tolerance:\nMirroring (RAID 1) ensures the data is duplicated. Even if one disk per mirrored pair fails, the array stays online.\nBest of both worlds:\nCombines RAID 0 speed with RAID 1 redundancy.",
      "RAID 10, also known as RAID 1+0, is a data storage technology that combines RAID 1 and RAID 0 to improve data protection and performance. It's a popular choice for high-end computing environments"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/153201-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-281-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 282,
    "question": "A data center has 4U rack servers that need to be replaced using VMs but without losing any data. Which of the following methods will MOST likely be used to replace these servers?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
