  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 289,
    "question": "A technician is tasked with upgrading 24 hosts simultaneously with a Type 1 hypervisor. Which of the following protocols should the technician use for this upgrade?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "VPN",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "TFTP",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "SSH",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "HTTP",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Network booting: TFTP is commonly used in the early stages of nodes booting from a local area network, such as in PXE (Preboot Execution Environment) deployments and for diskless workstations. TFTP is employed for uploading and downloading firmware images to network devices and embedded systems",
      "B. TFTP\nTFTP is often used for network booting and firmware upgrades.\n\nSSH provides secure connections and file transfers, but is not suitable for simultaneous distribution to large numbers of hosts.",
      "B. TFTP\nTFTP (Trivial File Transfer Protocol) is commonly used for lightweight file transfers in scenarios like firmware upgrades.",
      "its ssh"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/128731-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-289-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 290,
    "question": "A company is implementing a check-in desk to heighten physical security. Which of the following access controls would be the most appropriate to facilitate this implementation?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Security guards",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Security cameras",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Bollards",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "An access control vestibule",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Correct answer is A.\nFrom the CompTIA Server+ Student Guide:\nA security station enforces the management of visitors. The security desk provides guest badges, notifies employees that their guests have arrived, ensures that all visitors are properly escorted, and requires all visitors to sign in and sign out of the facility.",
      "You would check in with the security guards at the check in desk.",
      "D. An access control vestibule\n\nAn access control vestibule, also known as a mantrap, is specifically designed to control access to a secure area through a small, enclosed space with two or more doors. The design is such that the first door must close before the second door opens, ensuring that only authorized individuals can enter the secure area. It's a physical barrier that integrates with other security measures (like badges, biometrics, or PIN codes) to verify an individual's authorization before they can access the secure part of a building."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135841-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-290-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
