    ],
    "answers": [
      "I am going to vote E because its free (besides paying the empoyees) it does say cost effective.",
      "Correct answer is E, all other option are very cost-intensive.\nFrom CompTIA Server+ Student Guide:\nTabletop/Simulated failover—the disaster recovery procedures are implemented on a limited scale. Participants engage in role-playing to ensure comprehension and realism.",
      "Simulate and simulation are mentioned. Tabletop does not simulate. Tabletop is a discussion of a hypothetical situation and what could and should happen. Out of the remaining answers, B is the most cost effective to get this done.",
      "Tabletop isn't really a simulation. B is the correct answer."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/144533-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-295-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 296,
    "question": "The management team has mandated the encryption of all server administration traffic. Which of the following should most likely be implemented?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "SSH",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "VPN",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "SELinux",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "FTPS",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A. SSH\n\nWhy SSH?\nSecure Shell (SSH) provides encrypted command-line access and file transfer (via SCP/SFTP) to servers.\n\nIt’s the de facto standard for secure administrative sessions on both Linux and network devices.\n\nLightweight and easy to deploy—no need for additional VPN infrastructure if the goal is simply encrypting admin traffic.",
      "Wouldn't this be (D) FTPS?",
      "disregard, definitely SSH"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/169850-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-296-discussion/"
