  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 305,
    "question": "An administrator has been asked to disable CPU hyperthreading on a server to satisfy a licensing issue. Which of the following best describes how the administrator will likely perform this action?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Use an RDP/VNC session.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Modify the startup configuration.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Use a PowerShell/Bash script.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Use the BIOS/UEFI setup.",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "To disable CPU hyperthreading on a server, access your server's BIOS settings during boot, navigate to the processor options, and locate the \"Hyper-Threading\" setting, then change it from \"Enabled\" to \"Disabled\" and save the changes before exiting the BIOS; this process may vary slightly depending on your server's manufacturer and BIOS version."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/153237-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-305-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 306,
    "question": "Which of the following concepts refers to prioritizing a connection that had previously worked successfully?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Round robin",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "SCP",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "MRU",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Link aggregation",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. MRU\nMost Recently Used (MRU) best describes the concept of “prioritizing connections that have functioned successfully before.” This is a strategy that leverages past successful patterns to improve system efficiency and performance.",
      "MRU is most recently used",
      "D. Link aggregation:\nLink aggregation, also known as Ethernet bonding, link bundling, or port trunking, is the process of combining multiple network connections in parallel to increase throughput and redundancy. When a connection had previously worked successfully, link aggregation protocols such as LACP (Link Aggregation Control Protocol) or PAgP (Port Aggregation Protocol) may prioritize using that connection again, provided it's available and operational. This is typically achieved through load-balancing algorithms that take into account the status of each link and its past performance,. effectively prioritizing connections that have previously demonstrated reliability and success."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135842-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-306-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
