      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Replace the CMOS battery in the server.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Restart the time servers.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Manually correct the time.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "(A) Check the firewall rules.\n\nB *it's a VM, a CMOS battery is irrelevant.\nC *no, especially if everything else on the network is working.\nD *manually correcting would help temporarily, but you'd have to come back after it inevitably falls out-of-sync.",
      "A.\nFirewall could be blocking NTP"
    ],
