  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 311,
    "question": "A server administrator has been asked to implement a password policy that will help mitigate the chance of a successful brute-force attack. Which of the following password policies should the administrator implement first?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Lockout",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Length",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Complexity",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Minimum age",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Both would be amazing lockout and complexity, and choosing only one makes this wrong answer.\n\nBut since I can choose only one I would go with lockout.",
      "A. Lockout\n\nPassword complexity is irrelevant if the attacker has infinite attempts to guess the password (brute force).\nA lockout policy will allow only a specified number of attempts before the account is disabled, which stops the attack.",
      "Complexity",
      "A. Lockout\nlocking out accounts after a certain number of failed login attempts",
      "Complexity"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/134202-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-311-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 312,
    "question": "A storage engineer responds to an alarm on a storage array and finds the battery on the RAID controller needs to be replaced. However, the replacement part will not be available for 14 days. The engineer needs to identify the impact of the failed battery on the system. Which of the following best describes the impact?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The read and write performance will be impacted.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The read performance will be impacted.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The performance will not be impacted.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The write performance will be impacted.",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. The write performance will be impacted.\n\nRAID controllers often use a battery-backed cache (also known as write-back cache) to enhance performance. This cache temporarily stores write operations before they are written to the disk. The battery ensures that data in the cache can be retained and eventually written to the disk in the event of a power loss. If the battery on the RAID controller fails, the system may switch to write-through caching as a safety measure to prevent data loss. Write-through caching writes data directly to the disk without using the cache, which can significantly reduce write performance because it bypasses the performance benefits of the cache. Read performance is typically not directly affected by the status of the battery because data being read is not stored in the cache in the same way that write data is."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135844-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-312-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 313,
    "question": "An administrator discovers a misconfiguration that impacts all servers but can be easily corrected. The administrator has a list of affected servers and a script to correct the issue. Which of the following scripting principles should the administrator use to cycle through the list of servers to deliver the needed change?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Linked list",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "String",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Loop",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Constant",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. Loop\n\nA loop in scripting or programming is a control flow statement that allows code to be executed repeatedly based on a given condition or conditions. When dealing with a list of servers and needing to apply changes or execute a script on each server, a loop can iterate over the list, performing the required action(s) on each server until the list is exhausted. This method is efficient, reduces the potential for human error, and ensures that the change is consistently applied across all servers listed."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135845-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-313-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 314,
    "question": "A server administrator is configuring a new server in a data center in another country. Which of the following technologies should the administrator use to complete this task?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "IP KVM",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Crash cart",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Remote console",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Serial connection",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "I would go a here considering its a server and I will most likely need to access BIOS for RAID boot order and security.",
      "They are trying to trip you up between RDP and remote console (terminal access), IP KVM best answer.",
      "A. IP KVM\n\nIP KVM (Keyboard, Video, Mouse over IP) allows administrators to control a server remotely over the internet or a network, providing access to the server's console as if they were physically present. This technology is particularly useful when direct physical access to the server is not possible, such as in scenarios where the server is in a different country. It supports keyboard, video (monitor), and mouse input, enabling complete remote management capabilities, including BIOS access, system rebooting, and troubleshooting at the pre-OS level.",
      "Remote console\n\nRemote console technology enables administrators to access and manage servers from a remote location over a network connection. This allows for configuration, troubleshooting, and maintenance tasks to be performed without the need for physical access to the server's location.\n\nWhile options like IP KVM (Keyboard, Video, Mouse over IP) and serial connections can also provide remote access capabilities, a remote console often offers a more comprehensive and user-friendly interface for managing servers remotely"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/134244-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-314-discussion/"
  },
  {
