  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 321,
    "question": "An application needs 10GB of RAID 1 for log files, 20GB of RAID 5 for data files, and 20GB of RAID 5 for the operating system. All disks will be 10GB in capacity. Which of the following is the minimum number of disks needed for this application?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "6",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "7",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "8",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "9",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "For RAID 1 we need 2 disks as it works on mirrored volumes\nTo Calculate the Number of Disk for RAID 5, we need to calculate like this\nUseable Capacity = (Number of disks -1) x Disk Size Or\nUseabel Capaciity= (N-1) x Disk Size\nHere Useable Capacity = 20GB\nDisk Size = 10GB\nN=?\nPlace the values in the formula\n20GB = (N-1) x 10\n20GB = 10N-10\n10N =20+10\n10N = 30\nN = 3\nSame calculations will be performed for the 2nd RAID 5 array\nFinal calculation will be = 2 + 3 + 3=8",
      "For RAID 1 we need 2 disks as it works on mirrored volumes\nTo Calculate the Number of Disk for RAID 5, we need to calculate like this\nUseable Capacity = (Number of disks -1) x Disk Size Or\nUseabel Capaciity= (N-1) x Disk Size\nHere Useable Capacity = 20GB\nDisk Size = 10GB\nN=?\nPlace the values in the formula\n20GB = (N-1) x 10\n20GB = 10N-10\n10N =20+10\n10N = 30\nN = 3\nSame calculations will be performed for the 2nd RAID 5 array\nFinal calculation will be = 2 + 3 + 3=8",
      "RAID 1 for Log Files: 2 disks\nRAID 5 for Data Files: 3 disks\nRAID 5 for Operating System: 3 disks",
      "C is not correct, it does not specify that the 2x 20gb of Raid5 need to be on separate arrays so it is 2 disk for the raid1 = 10gb and 5 disk of raid5 = 40gb.",
      "C. 8 Disks (per AzadOB's explanation)",
      "To calculate the minimum number of disks needed for the given RAID configurations, let's break down each requirement:\n\nRAID 1 for log files: This requires mirroring, so each disk contributes half of its capacity. Since we need a total of 10GB usable space, we'll need 20GB raw capacity (10GB mirrored). Thus, we need 20GB / 10GB = 2 disks.\n\nRAID 5 for data files (20GB): RAID 5 requires at least three disks, and one disk worth of capacity is used for parity. So, for 20GB of usable space, we'll need 3 disks.\n\nRAID 5 for the operating system (20GB): Same as the data files, we'll need 3 disks for 20GB of usable space.\n\nAdding these up:\n\nRAID 1 (log files): 2 disks\nRAID 5 (data files): 3 disks\nRAID 5 (operating system): 3 disks\n\nTotal disks needed: 2 + 3 + 3 = 8 disks.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\nC. 8"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/134247-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-321-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 322,
    "question": "Which of the following backup methods protects all the changes that have occurred since the last full backup?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Incremental",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Archive",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Differential",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Snapshot",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. Differential\n\nONLY backs up data since last full backup. Chat GPT says A but that backs up data since last incremental backup OR full backup"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/129113-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-322-discussion/"
  },
