  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 332,
    "question": "After installing an OS on a new server, the administrator realizes the server does not have any network connectivity. The administrator checks the network cable, and it seems to be transferring data. Which of the following should be checked next?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "NIC firmware",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "IPv4 options",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "DHCP options",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Firewall options",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "E",
        "text": "DNS settings",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "It should be B, very few server deployments use DHCP. If they want that to be the answer they would need to specify the servers receive their IPs via DHCP since that is an atypical setup.",
      "B. IPv4 options\n\nChecking the IPv4 options involves ensuring the server is correctly configured to communicate on the network, including having a valid IP address, subnet mask, and default gateway. These settings can be assigned manually or obtained automatically through DHCP. If these settings are not correctly configured, the server will not be able to communicate on the network, even if the physical connection (network cable) is functioning correctly."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135850-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-332-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 333,
    "question": "A technician needs to replace two RAID controllers on a database server as part of an upgrade. The server has six external storage arrays and eight internal disks that are controlled by the two RAID controllers. The technician completes the replacement and powers the systems back on, but the server OS detects several missing disks in the configuration. Which of the following steps should the technician take first to resolve this issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Reboot to the RAID controller BIOS and rescan for attached disks and arrays.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Start the motherboard UEFI and confirm the RAID controller start order is correct.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Turn off the external arrays and reboot the server to redetect the internal disks first.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Turn off all components and confirm all external and internal cables before rebooting.",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A. appears to be the most correct and the option actually addressing the one potential mis-match in installing new hardware.\nEverything else describes checking equipment that was either working just fine before the hardware upgrade (that wasn't touched) or was never changed before or after the upgrade.",
      "Checking every single cable is time intensive and may be unnecessary. A is going to be the fastest option to see what drives aren't connected, and if the issue is between the Drives and the RAID controller, which is what D is \"fixing\" or if the issue is between the RAID controller and the OS."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/149421-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-333-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 334,
    "question": "A technician is provisioning a 4TB LUN on a SAN for a Windows server. Which of the following filesystem types should be used for this server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "ZFS",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "FAT",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "VMFS",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "ReFS",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "D. ReFS (Resilient File System)\n\nReFS is designed by Microsoft to maximize data availability, scale efficiently to large data sets across diverse workloads, and provide data integrity with resiliency to corruption. It's particularly well-suited for large volumes, making it an ideal choice for a 4TB LUN. ReFS is compatible with Windows Server operating systems and is designed to work with data storage solutions such as SANs."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135858-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-334-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
