  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 346,
    "question": "Which of the following testing exercises for disaster recovery is primarily used to discuss incident response strategies for critical systems without affecting production data?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Tabletop",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Backup recovery test",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Live failover",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Hot-site visit audit",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A tabletop exercise is a discussion‑based, non‑intrusive disaster recovery (DR) test where team members walk through incident response strategies without touching production systems or data.\nIt is specifically designed to:\n\nReview critical system response plans\nDiscuss roles, communication flow, and decision‑making\nAvoid any operational impact because no systems are powered down or altered"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/339329-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-346-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 347,
    "question": "A server technician is placing a newly configured server into a corporate environment. The server will be used by members of the accounting department, who are currently assigned by the VLAN identified below:\n\n\n\nWhich of the following IP address configurations should the technician assign to the new server so the members of the accounting group can access the server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "IP address: 172.16.25.90/24 -\nDefault gateway: 172.16.25.254",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "IP address: 172.16.25.101/16 -\nDefault gateway: 172.16.25.254",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "IP address: 172.16.25.254/24 -\nDefault gateway: 172.16.25.1",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "IP address: 172.16.26.101/24 -\nDefault gateway: 172.16.25.254",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A. IP address: 172.16.25.90/24 -\nDefault gateway: 172.16.25.254\n\nVLAN NAME: ACCOUNTING\nVLAN ID: 25\nIP ADDRESS: 172.16.25.1 - 172.16.25.254/24\nDEFAULT GATEWAY: 172.16.25.254\nEXCLUSION RANGE: 172.16.25.50 - 172.a6.25.100\n\nBased on the scenario provided, none of the options work (at a glance). Therefore, (unless there is a typo) I will make the assumption this question is not about IP addressing, it is about understanding the rationales behind administrative practices such as Exclusion Ranges. An exclusion range is typically created for use by only certain types of hosts, like servers or printers. Based on that rationale, assigning the server an IP address from the exclusion range is the BEST answer.",
      ".90 is part of the exclusion rang so A is not the answer. B is dumb because why would they use vlans and a /16 but since they don't specify a subnet mask, it is the only right answer.\nC is wrong because you're assigning it the gateway IP. D is wrong because it is on the wrong subnet .26,",
      "fwiw this is very poorly worded questions. For all we know the exclusion range is on another subnet.",
      "Meant to say VLAN not subnet",
      "Generally we assign a server a static IP and ensure that its in the DHCP exclusion range so there is no IP conflicts. It would make sense to use an IP from the exclusion range"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135944-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-347-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 348,
