  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 352,
    "question": "Which of the following is an architectural reinforcement that is used to attempt to conceal the exterior of an organization?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Fencing",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Bollards",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Camouflage",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Reflective glass",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "I believe the correct answer is C – Camouflage. My reasoning is that reflective glass would conceal the interior of the organization, whereas the question specifically refers to concealing the exterior. Based on that wording, camouflage seems like the more appropriate choice.",
      "camouflage is the term for this purpose"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/312894-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-352-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 353,
    "question": "A server administrator is installing a new server with multiple NICs on it. The Chief Information Officer has asked the administrator to ensure the new server will have the least amount of network downtime but a good amount of network speed. Which of the following best describes what the administrator should implement on the new server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "VLAN",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "vNIC",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Link aggregation",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Failover",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "NIC teaming with link aggregation (802.3ad LACP)",
      "C. Link aggregation\n\nLink aggregation, also known as NIC teaming or bonding, allows multiple network interfaces to be combined into a single logical interface to increase throughput and provide redundancy. This configuration provides both increased network speed and fault tolerance, reducing the risk of network downtime. Therefore, implementing link aggregation would best meet the requirements outlined by the Chief Information Officer."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135956-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-353-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 354,
    "question": "The management team has mandated the use of data-at-rest encryption for all data. Which of the following forms of encryption best achieves this goal?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Drive",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Database",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Folder",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "File",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A. Drive\n\nEncrypting the entire storage drive (such as a hard drive or solid-state drive) is the most comprehensive approach to achieving data-at-rest encryption. This method ensures that all data stored on the drive, regardless of the file type or location, is encrypted. It provides a high level of security by protecting the data at the storage level itself, making it inaccessible to unauthorized users even if the physical storage device is stolen or compromised."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135957-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-354-discussion/"
  },
