  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 357,
    "question": "A new application server has been configured in the cloud to provide access to all clients within the network. On-site users are able to access all resources, but remote users are reporting issues connecting to the new application. The server administrator verifies that all users are configured with the appropriate group memberships. Which of the following is most likely causing the issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Telnet connections are disabled on the server.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Role-based access control is misconfigured.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "There are misconfigured firewall rules.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Group policies have not been applied.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. There are misconfigured firewall rules.\n\nWhen users access resources from within the local network (on-site), they typically do not encounter the same firewall restrictions as remote users. However, remote users often need to traverse network boundaries, which may involve passing through firewalls or other network security devices."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135959-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-357-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 358,
    "question": "A company recently implemented VoIP across a multicampus environment with ten locations. The company uses many network technologies, including fiber, copper, and wireless. Users calling between three of the locations have reported that voices sound strange. Which of the following should be monitored to narrow down the issue?",
    "options": [
