        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Replace the fans.",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Assuming several servers in different racks are noisy, so in order to monitor them, the technician may establish the remote connections to all of them instead of changing fans. But who chooses the answers in Examtopics, this is questionable",
      "C. Establish a remote connection to the server.\n\nThis approach enables the technician to perform a preliminary assessment and potentially pinpoint the cause of the noise without immediately resorting to physical interventions that may disrupt server operations. Once the source of the noise is identified through logs or hardware status reports, the technician can decide on the appropriate course of action, whether it involves replacing specific components or adjusting configurations to mitigate the noise.",
      "Wouldn't you check the fans?"
