  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 377,
    "question": "A site is considered a warm site when it:",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "has basic technical facilities connected to it.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "has faulty air conditioning that is awaiting service.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "is almost ready to take over all operations from the primary site.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "is fully operational and continuously providing services.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "C. is almost ready to take over all operations from the primary site.\n\nWarm sites are disaster recovery solutions that have the necessary telecommunications and IT infrastructure but do not have live data. Equipment, including servers and networking hardware, may be present but not fully configured. Warm sites require a short period to become fully operational, making them a middle ground between the faster recovery times of a hot site (which is fully operational and continuously providing services) and the slower recovery time of a cold site (which has basic facilities but no technology until moved there)."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135969-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-377-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 378,
    "question": "An administrator is working locally in a data center with multiple server racks. Which of the following is the best low-cost option to connect to any server while on site?",
