  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 381,
    "question": "A server administrator deployed a new product that uses a non-standard port for web access on port 8443. However, users are unable to access the new application. The server administrator checks firewall rules and determines 8443 is allowed. Which of the following is most likely the cause of the issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Intrusion detection is blocking the port.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The new application's DNS entry is incorrect.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The application should be changed to use port 443.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The core switch has a network issue.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "This is most likely a DNS configuration of the new server that was deployed.",
      "A. Intrusion detection is blocking the port.\n\nIntrusion Detection Systems (IDS) or Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS) often monitor network traffic for suspicious activities and can block access to ports based on security policies or detected anomalies. If the IDS/IPS was not configured to recognize traffic on port 8443 as legitimate, it might automatically block access to this port, even if the firewall rules allow it.",
      "You are lame.... IDS is just alert-based and wouldn't prevent the connection from being established.",
      "bro all you use is ChatGPT and don't use any personal reasoning. IDS = Intrusion DETECTION System NOT a PREVENTIVE system.",
      "Yeah i know right"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/135972-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-381-discussion/"
  },
