  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 385,
    "question": "SIMULATION\n-\n\nUsers report that the FinanceApp software is not running, and they need immediate access. Issues with the FinanceApp software occur every week after the IT team completes server system updates. The users, however, do not want to contact the help desk every time the issue occurs.\n\nThe users also report the new MarketApp software is not usable when it crashes, which can cause significant downtime. The technician who restarted the MarketApp software noticed it is running under a test account, which is a likely cause of the crashes.\n\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n-\n\nUsing the Services menu provided, modify the appropriate application services to remedy the stated issues.\n\nIf at any time you would like to bring back the initial state of the simulation, please click the Reset All button.",
    "options": [],
    "suggested_answers": [],
    "answers": [
      "FinanceApp Service:\n\n- Set the FinanceApp Service to automatically restart if it stops. This ensures the service is always running after system updates.\n\n- Change the startup type to Automatic if it is not already set. This ensures the service starts automatically after a reboot.\n\nMarketApp Service:\n\n- Change the MarketApp Service to run under a more appropriate account instead of a test account. Typically, this should be a service account with the necessary permissions.\n\n- Set the startup type to Automatic to ensure it starts automatically and reduces downtime."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/143712-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-385-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 386,
    "question": "A server located in an IDF of a paper mill reboots every other day at random times. Which of the following should the technician perform on the server first?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Check the power cables.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Clean the fans.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Replace the RAM.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Reattach the CPU heat sink.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "A keyword word is randomly.",
      "it doesnt matter if the server is located at papermill or any building. it is asking what should the tech do FIRST? The first thing is to check power cables because server being randomly rebooting causes some hardware failures(including fans) but what should you do as a technician first?\nwell as a tech, i ll look for event logs or some link lights but since the options are limited here so the best answer among all is A",
      "Because a paper mill is a very dusty environment, even the \"clean\" areas (offices, IT spaces, etc) are going to be \"dirty.\" Cleaning the fans is probably the best place to start. It's really kind of a toss-up, since it could be a faulty power cable arcing after it warms up enough due to current flow, or it could be the server shutting off after it gets too hot because the fans are caked in debris. Not a great question, and an excellent example of why I dislike CompTIA questions.",
      "Obviously B overheating",
      "A is simplest and most likely solution"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/140929-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-386-discussion/"
  },
