  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 396,
    "question": "An employee who was dismissed did not return company-issued equipment. Which of the following is the most important information the IT department needs to give to the legal department?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Labeling",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Serial number",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Warranty",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Asset tag",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Asset tag",
      "facepalm..... Thank you sir for the enlightenment!!!",
      "The serial number is associated with an asset tag. The asset tag can be altered or removed easier than the SN.",
      "I think the asset tag is correct because it proves that the company owns the asset.",
      "have you ever purchased an electronic? The BOL mentions the SN, which is a manufacturer-generated code that identifies the product uniquely. An asset tag is placed by the company IT team to track assets internally. When the device is stolen (or not returned such as in this case), the asset tag can be taken off since that's just the sticker. The SN of the device is embedded in the system configuration and can always be found in the settings."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/149193-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-396-discussion/"
  },
