  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 406,
    "question": "A DHCP server was installed on the network and duplicate IP addresses are being assigned. The administrator decides to manually account for IP addresses and remove the DHCP services. However, clients are still being assigned IP addresses. Which of the following would be the best option to resolve this issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Checking the DHCP server for reservations",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Checking the lease time of the IP address",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Checking the DHCP server for unexpired leases",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Checking and scanning for any rogue DHCP servers within the network",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Its not as simple as in seems:\nConsider a situation where DHCP server allots (lets say IP 105.62.118.150) with 7 days lease. On the same day, admin turned off DHCP and started allocating static IP. There are chances that the admin assigns another device the same IP? In this case, wouldn't both the devices have the same IP?",
      "Locate and disable the rogue DHCP server (unauthorized DHCP source)."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/336934-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-406-discussion/"
  },
