  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 412,
    "question": "Following a recent power outage, a server on a server farm has been running slowly. A technician receives a ticket with a request to check for anything out of the ordinary. The technician sees an orange light on the front console of the server, indicating an error. Which of the following should the technician check next?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "CPU",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Power supply",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "RAM",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "RAID battery",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "An orange light (sometimes amber or yellow) on the front panel of a server typically indicates a hardware alert or degraded status. After a power outage, if the server is running slowly and there's an error light, a degraded RAID array is a likely cause. This can happen if the RAID controller’s battery backup unit (BBU) has failed or is in a learning cycle, which affects write caching and performance.\n\nTherefore, the RAID battery is the most likely component to check next.",
      "Considering servers usually have redundant power supply's I don't think this would cause the system to any run any different. I would go with Raid battery here."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/154620-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-412-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 413,
