  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 417,
    "question": "A software developer is unable to reach an internal website. The developer's attempt to ping the FQDN returns the following IP address: 104.18.17.32. Which of the following is the most likely reason for this result?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "The NIC is set to DHCP.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The default gateway is misconfigured.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The primary DNS server is 8.8.8.8.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "There is a manual entry in the hosts file.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The ping to an \"internal\" website should not be returning a public IP address unless it's FQDN was manually set that way. (D)",
      "D. There is a manual entry in the hosts file.\n\nThe most likely cause of this issue is having your external IP address manually configured in your hosts file."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/151264-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-417-discussion/"
  },
