  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 423,
    "question": "A technician is configuring a new server with four disks for the development team. The requirements are disk redundancy and maximum usable disk capacity. Which of the following RAID levels should be used for this server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "0",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "1",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "5",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "10",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "0 = no redundnacy\n1 = 2 available disks\n3 = 3 available disks + 1 for parity"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/152763-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-423-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 424,
    "question": "A technician is setting up a repurposed server. The minimum requirements are 2TB while ensuring the highest performance and providing support for one drive failure. The technician has the following six drives available:\n\n\n\nWhich of the following drive selections should the technician utilize to best accomplish this goal?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "1, 2, 4, and 6",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "1, 2, 3, 5, and 6",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "1, 2, 4, 5, and 6",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "1, 2, 3, 4, and 6",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Correct answer is C I was wrong",
      "To meet the requirements of 2TB capacity, high performance, and support for one drive failure, the technician should configure the drives in a RAID 10 (1+0) setup. RAID 10 provides:\n\nHigh performance: Combines the speed of striping (RAID 0) with redundancy (RAID 1).\nSupport for one drive failure: Data is mirrored, so a single drive failure does not result in data loss.",
      "My first thought was A. But going with C. RAID 5 drives don't have to be identical, better performance, single disk failure and the added drive number 6 for for failure would keep the usable storage at 2TB."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/150644-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-424-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 425,
    "question": "An administrator is troubleshooting a server that is rebooting and crashing. The administrator notices that the server is making sounds that are louder than usual. Upon closer inspection, the administrator discovers that the noises are coming from the front of the chassis. Which of the following is the most likely reason for this behavior?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "One of the fans has failed.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "The power supply has failed.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "The RAM is malfunctioning.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "The CPU is overheating.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Most likely reason for which behavior? Rebooting and crashing or Making loader than usual sounds?",
      "When it is making a loud noise, the answer can only be A.\nA fan can make an unusual noise due to dust buildup, or it can make a loud noise due to a malfunction."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/150645-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-425-discussion/"
  },
