  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 428,
    "question": "A server administrator is setting up a disk with enforcement policies on how much data each home share can hold. The amount of data that is redundant on the server must also be minimized. Which of the following should the administrator perform on the server? (Choose two.)",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Partitioning",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Deduplication",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Disk quotas",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Compression",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "E",
        "text": "Cloning",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "F",
        "text": "Provisioning",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B",
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Disk quota\nDeduplication",
      "Disk quotas allow the administrator to enforce policies on how much data each home share can hold. This feature enables setting limits on the amount of disk space that users or groups can use, which directly addresses the requirement to control data allocation for home shares\nDeduplication is a technique that minimizes redundant data on the server by identifying and eliminating duplicate copies of repeating data. This process significantly reduces storage consumption, meeting the requirement to minimize redundant data on the server.",
      "\"enforcement policies on how much each home share can hold\" = (C) Disk quotas\n\"the amount of data that is redundant on the server must be minimized\" = (B) Deduplication\n\n*Compression would only trim the file size down not minimize the redundant data",
      "I would go with B & C. Compression only shrinks file sizes."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/150646-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-428-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 429,
    "question": "A server administrator needs to ensure proprietary data does not leave the company. Which of the following should the administrator implement to meet this requirement?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "A review of users' activities",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "File-level monitoring",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "A SIEM solution",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "A DLP policy",
        "is_correct": true
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The correct answer is D. A DLP policy.\n\nHere's why:\n\nDLP (Data Loss Prevention) is specifically designed to detect, monitor, and prevent the unauthorized transfer of sensitive or proprietary data outside of the company.\n\nIt can block or alert on activities like:\n\nCopying data to a USB drive\n\nSending sensitive documents via email",
      "(D) A Data LOSS Prevention policy\n\n*reviewing users' activities to prevent this would be an overwhelming and near impossible task.",
      "D. A DLP policy\n\nDLP can prevent sensitive data from being leaked and is a powerful solution for protecting a company's critical information assets."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/151296-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-429-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
