  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 439,
    "question": "A senior administrator was notified that a junior administrator installed software on a server that should not have new software installed on it. The senior administrator decides to restrict the server via a Group Policy. Which of the following can be used to elevate the permissions?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Computer management",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "AD",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Local users and groups",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "UAC",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The correct answer is D. UAC (User Account Control).\n\nExplanation:\n\nUAC is a Windows security feature that helps prevent unauthorized changes by prompting for administrative approval before allowing elevated actions (like installing software).\n\nEven if a Group Policy restricts regular users from installing software, UAC would prompt for elevated permissions (an administrator password) to complete the action.\n\nIn this case, restricting software installation would work with UAC enforcement, ensuring only users with the right credentials could elevate permissions and install anything."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/303067-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-439-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 440,
    "question": "A technician is investigating a server's configuration to secure it from physical threats. The technician checks the BIOS and sees the following boot order:\n\n\nUSB Drive -\n\nCDROM Drive -\n\nNetwork Adapter -\n\nRAID Controller -\n\nAdditionally, the server's host OS is stored on mirrored drives. Which of the following should the technician do to secure the server?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Disable all except RAID Controller.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Block USB ports on the server.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Set BIOS password.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Move RAID Controller to the top of the list.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "The correct answer is: A. Disable all except RAID Controller.\n\nHere's why:\nThe current boot order allows the server to boot from USB, CDROM, or network before the RAID controller (which holds the actual OS on mirrored drives). This creates a security vulnerability, as an attacker with physical access could boot from a USB or CD and bypass the installed OS to access or manipulate data.\n\nBy disabling all boot options except the RAID Controller, the technician ensures that the server can only boot from the internal drives, significantly reducing the risk of booting into unauthorized environments.",
      "I concur"
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/303620-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-440-discussion/"
  },
  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 441,
