  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 443,
    "question": "A systems administrator is provisioning a large number of virtual Linux machines that will be configured identically. The administrator would like to configure the machines quickly and easily but does not have access to an automation/orchestration platform. Additionally, the administrator would like to set up a system that can be used in the future, even on newer versions of the OS. Which of the following will best meet the administrator's requirements?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Deploying each server from a VM template",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Using a kickstart file during installation",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Configuring each server manually one at a time",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Copying/pasting configuration commands into each server through SSH sessions",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "E",
        "text": "Configuring a single server and then creating clones of it",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "Please don't comment and vote if you have no idea what the hell you are talking about. B is the answer because Kickstart likes are designed for automating.",
      "I'm not going with B simply because it's not listed on the exam objectives. I'm not choosing E because there are a lot of extra steps involved when cloning a VM in a production environment."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/163727-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-443-discussion/"
  },
