  {
    "exam_code": "sk0-005",
    "topic": 1,
    "question_num": 446,
    "question": "A technician notices that every time a server is powered on, it turns off after several minutes. After reviewing logs, the technician notices the server registers execution of the shutdown. Which of the following should the technician do to fix this issue?",
    "options": [
      {
        "letter": "A",
        "text": "Reset the memory modules.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "B",
        "text": "Check for fan failure.",
        "is_correct": true
      },
      {
        "letter": "C",
        "text": "Change the VM password.",
        "is_correct": false
      },
      {
        "letter": "D",
        "text": "Set credentials for the remote console.",
        "is_correct": false
      }
    ],
    "suggested_answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "answers": [
      "I know B is the correct answer with the fan issue but OMG i hate CompTIA for wording their questions. I have an active A+, N+, Sec+, and PenTest+ for the last 8 years and have always hated CompTIA for their question wording. \"server registers execution of the shutdown\" also means \"someone issued a remote shutdown command.\""
    ],
    "url": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/comptia/view/336152-exam-sk0-005-topic-1-question-446-discussion/"
  },
